Marie (docs): Quick heads-up — PR #482 updated streaming examples to show resume tokens + pagination. We forgot to add the Go example and a short note about idempotency. Can someone take a pass?

Sam (sdk): On it. I pushed python + ts changes in my branch but left TODO for Go.

Jon (eng): What was the root issue we discovered again?

Sam (sdk): When a stream fails mid-page and client retries from the last cursor, some sample code replays items because token counting/offset was mixed with resume token semantics. We need explicit resume-token usage, not rely on offsets.

Dave (docs-review): TL;DR: add small examples for all 3 langs showing a) how to capture resume token b) how to retry with exponential backoff c) how to avoid duplicate results when rejoining a paginated stream. Keep each snippet ~6 lines.

Luis (sdk): Draft Python snippet I used in PR:```python
# capture resume token and retry
def stream_items(client, cursor=None):
    for chunk in client.stream_list(cursor=cursor):
        if "resume_token" in chunk:
            cursor = chunk["resume_token"]
        yield from chunk.get("items", [])

# on retry: pass last saved cursor
items = list(stream_items(client, cursor=saved_cursor))
```

Ada (infra): Nice. Add a note that resume_token is stable across restarts only for the same model+route; otherwise fall back to earliest.

Sam (sdk): TS snippet I added:```ts
// async iterator with resume token
async function* streamItems(client, cursor?: string) {
  for await (const part of client.streamList({ cursor })) {
    if (part.resume_token) cursor = part.resume_token;
    yield* (part.items ?? []);
  }
}
// callers should persist cursor before processing next page
```

Jon (eng): Can we show Go too? Many infra customers ask for Go + retry example. Keep it sync-style for brevity.

Luis (sdk): I'll draft a concise Go example and push to the PR:```go
// resume token + retry example (pseudo)
func StreamItems(client *sdk.Client, cursor string) ([]Item, error) {
  for {
    resp, err := client.StreamList(ctx, &ListParams{Cursor: cursor})
    if err != nil {
      // retry/backoff and continue (preserve cursor)
      backoff.Wait()
      continue
    }
    if resp.ResumeToken != "" { cursor = resp.ResumeToken }
    return resp.Items, nil
  }
}
```

Dave (docs-review): Couple of editorial points: 1) call out idempotency guarantee: "resume token is a replay-safe cursor for the live stream" 2) small callout on cost/latency when resuming mid-sequence 3) link to the SDK section about backoff helpers.

Marie (docs): Also add an inline note near the top: "If you need strict de-duplication, persist seen IDs server-side; resume tokens aim to minimize but may not be deduplicated by default."

Sam (sdk): Will add the note + link to backoff helper (sdk/docs/retries.md).

